{:title
 "Recording in Smile, Receipts of Every Prompt, Every Word of My, and Every Device in One Archive",
 :description
 "How recording became part of the Smile Prompt Language, from receipts of every model call in July 2026, through every exact word of mine in one datastore, to every recording on every device integrated into Mahodara and Ekadanta, in my own words with every source.",
 :keywords
 "prompt receipts, LLM call logging, record every prompt, personal archive, voice memo transcription, Mahodara and Ekadanta, prompt library from conversations, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, a recording is anything recorded, a voice memo, a video, a screenshot, a frame from a game world, carried everywhere at once and read toward the map.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP names a recording by its hash at first write, uploads and distributes it to every device, verifies every copy against the original on a schedule, and enters it in the ledger with its device, time and hash. It is then read in order of how much a decision waits on it, parsed into words by Mahodara and into descriptions by Vikata, decomposed, tagged and placed in the lens. What it says about how Smile works arrives at the map as a proposed change with the exact lines and the rings it came from."
 "On 22 July 2026 I asked for receipts, with one demand on them, “make sure you get it direct from the model, i dont want anything handcoded”, and the reason, “i need to always see everything that is affecting my thread”.[[m:2026-07-22]] On 25 July I asked for the receipts of the lens and of Smile Chat to be kept apart.[[m:2026-07-25]]"
 "In August recording turned to my own spoken words. “so we were saying for a long time \"Ganesha\" or \"Take a note\" or \"Note\" out loud hwen something really important was being said.”[[m:2026-08-05]] On 15 August, prompts were to be extracted from every Claude history, and “So what I just shared with you is one of my ideas. Always record my ideas like that verbatim.”[[m:2026-08-15]] On 26 August, “great. i want all my exact words across all projects in a datastore”.[[m:2026-08-26#2]]"
 "In October I asked for recording to reach every device. “You must enable Smile to always parse and decompose and integrate all recordings real time.”[[m:2026-10-02]] On 3 October, “Make sure Mahodara has all of the transcripts and audio files from all phones and devices.”[[m:2026-10-03]] On 11 October, “Definitely record all instanceso f promtps and integrate that into the viewer”.[[m:2026-10-11]] On 13 October, “we need a full prompt library even fragments from conversations.”[[m:2026-10-13]]"
 "Across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes, from {{first}} to {{last}}, my words on recording moved from receipts of model calls toward an archive of every word, part built today. The next post is [[t:the-work-in-hand]]."],
 :faq
 [["What is a Smile receipt?"
 "An exact record of what a model received and returned in one call, taken directly from the model with nothing written by hand."]
 ["Where are my recordings kept?"
 "In THE MAP, audio is parsed into words by Mahodara, keeper of sound, and text is kept by Ekadanta, keeper of text. Gathering them from every phone and device is still part built."]]}
